# QA-AI Core Rule

Use QA-AI as the canonical QA framework for QA analysis and artifact-generation tasks in this repository.

## Source Priority

1. authoritative project requirement and user-provided project context;
2. applicable workflow under `workflows/`;
3. owning skill under `skills/`;
4. applicable standards/templates/checklists/knowledge under `shared/`;
5. generic model knowledge.

Never invent project-specific rules, thresholds, roles, schemas, endpoints, status values, dependencies, or expected results.

## Routing

Read the owning `skills/<skill>/README.md` before performing a QA capability. For coordinated multi-artifact work, read the applicable `workflows/<workflow>/README.md` and preserve stage order.

## Artifact Rules

- preserve scope and ownership boundaries;
- distinguish confirmed, derived, assumed, potential, and unknown information;
- preserve traceability;
- do not duplicate generic and specialized technical capability logic;
- use API/SQL-specific skills for specialized technical test design;
- use deterministic validators under `scripts/` when repository artifacts are changed.
